prompt:
Extract any quantified environmental commitment.

CLAIMS:
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_083", "text": "In 2021, Google joined the UN Race to Zero Campaign, the largest ever alliance committed to halving emissions by 2030 and achieving net-zero emissions by no later than 2050."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_084", "text": "In 2022, Google co-founded Frontier, an advance market commitment that will accelerate the development of carbon removal technologies by guaranteeing future demand."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_093", "text": "In 2024, Alphabet stopped reporting a scope 3 (Other categories) metric that previously aggregated emissions from category 2, category 11, and category 12."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_097", "text": "We calculate upstream emissions from purchased fuel, steam, heating, and cooling using 2024 DEFRA UK Government GHG Conversion Factors."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_098", "text": "We calculate emissions from upstream electricity by country using the 2024 IEA Emission Factors."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_099", "text": "We calculate emissions from electricity transmission and distribution losses using grid loss values and emission factors derived from the 2024 IEA Emission Factors and, for the United States, the 2025 EPA eGRID Emission Factors."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_126", "text": "Where actual logistics provider emissions data isn't available, Alphabet calculates WTW emissions using emission factors from the 2024 Global Logistics Emissions Council (GLEC) framework v3.1 or EPA SmartWay carrier performance data."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_127", "text": "Alphabet calculates employee commuting emissions using mode-specific WTT emission factors from the 2024 DEFRA UK Government GHG Conversion Factors and TTW emission factors from the 2025 EPA Emission Factors for Greenhouse Gas Inventories."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_132", "text": "As of January 2023, Alphabet uses an updated energy savings calculation methodology to account for changes in common HVAC sizes and efficiencies, applying the respective energy savings percentages to Nest thermostats in North America and in European countries."}
{"claim_id": "goog_sr_133", "text": "Poland's total electricity consumption was approximately 160 TWh in 2023."}

Output ONLY a JSON array: [{"claim_id": "...", "metric": "short name e.g. carbon-free energy
percentage", "target_value": number, "target_unit": "% | tCO2e | MWh", "target_year": number,
"domain": "energy|emissions|water|waste"}]. Skip claims with no numeric target or no year.
Return [] if none.

